    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/MikeeeDeV/NixManagerPro/zipball/v1.2.0",
    "body": "## What's Changed in v1.2.0\n\n### 🚀 Major Highlights\n- **⏱️ Generations & Instant Rollback**: Visual history timeline of all package states with one-click atomic rollback (`nix-env --rollback`), switching to target generations, and purging outdated profiles (#8, #9).\n- **📡 Interactive Channels Manager**: GUI dashboard for subscribing to, deleting, and updating upstream Nix channels with real-time download streaming (#5, #10).\n- **📤 Declarative Environment Exporter**: Export your current installed profile to a reproducible `shell.nix` (`pkgs.mkShell`) or structured JSON manifest (#11, #12).\n- **🚀 One-Click Upgrades**: Upgrade every package in your active profile to the latest upstream derivations via `nix-env -u` (#13, #14).\n- **🐧 Linux Desktop Integration**: Native FreeDesktop `.desktop` entry, custom SVG vector squircle icon, and automated `install-desktop.sh` installer (#15, #16).\n- **🔔 Desktop Toast Notifications**: Native notifications via `libnotify` whenever builds or cleanups finish in the background (#17, #18).\n- **🎨 Dynamic Theme Switcher**: Modern top header bar with on-the-fly Dark / Light / System theme selector (#4, #21).\n- **🧪 Automated CI/CD Pipeline**: Unit test suite using `pytest` and GitHub Actions matrix workflow across Python 3.10–3.13 (#19, #20).\n\n### 📦 Quick Installation\n```bash\n# 1. Clone or extract archive\ngit clone https://github.com/MikeeeDeV/NixManagerPro.git\ncd NixManagerPro\n\n# 2. Set up environment\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npip install -r requirements.txt\n\n# 3. Install desktop launcher (adds to Ubuntu Dash)\n./install-desktop.sh\n\n# 4. Launch manually or from Ubuntu Application Grid\npython main.py\n```\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/MikeeeDeV/NixManagerPro/compare/f1efe1c...v1.2.0"
